{"id":"TILSKUD2","text":"Directly subsidies in agriculture","description":"Directly subsidies in agriculture by grant type and time","unit":"m DKK","suppressedDataValue":"0","updated":"2026-05-19T08:00:00","active":true,"contacts":[{"name":"Simone Thun","phone":"+4551369251","mail":"sit@dst.dk"}],"documentation":{"id":"a9fe5dae-435f-4ac2-9133-35e21a72cd0e","url":"https://www.dst.dk/documentationofstatistics/a9fe5dae-435f-4ac2-9133-35e21a72cd0e"},"footnote":{"text":"The table shows the total amounts paid out via the Agency for Green Transition and Aquatic Environment&apos;s subsidy schemes. Subsidies paid via 3.3. Market Support and 4.4. Wetlands, as well as a portion of 4.8. Other subsidy schemes, do not go to primary producers. \r\nThe amounts indicate the year in which the subsidies were paid, not necessarily the year to which the payments refer. The latest two years are provisional","mandatory":false},"variables":[{"id":"TILSKUDSART","text":"grant type","elimination":true,"time":false,"values":[{"id":"300","text":"GENERAL SUBSIDIES, TOTAL"},{"id":"305","text":"Direct payment, total (1+2+3)"},{"id":"310","text":"1 Basic payment and green support"},{"id":"315","text":"2 Eco-schemes, total"},{"id":"325","text":"2.1 Biodiversity and sustainability"},{"id":"330","text":"2.2 Climate and environmentally friendly grass"},{"id":"335","text":"2.3 Extensive farming with mowing"},{"id":"340","text":"2.4 Varied plant production"},{"id":"345","text":"2.5 Organic area support"},{"id":"350","text":"3 Other direct payment, total"},{"id":"355","text":"3.1 Product-related subsidies"},{"id":"360","text":"3.2 Young farmers"},{"id":"365","text":"3.3 Market support"},{"id":"370","text":"3.4 Other direct payment"},{"id":"375","text":"4 Other schemes, total"},{"id":"380","text":"4.1 Natura 2000"},{"id":"385","text":"4.2 Targeted regulation"},{"id":"390","text":"4.3 Organic area subsidies and investments"},{"id":"395","text":"4.4 Wetlands"},{"id":"400","text":"4.5 Establishment support fo